Make VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER cover the drafter's candidate top-k, which it does not.

kind: fix. Retires when upstream takes it.

VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0 reads as "do not use FlashInfer for sampling", and
topk_topp_sampler.py:45 honours it. _flashinfer_topk() in logits_processor.py does not: it
gates only on current_platform.is_cuda() and has_flashinfer(), so the switch is half a
kill-switch. The drafter reaches it unconditionally -- Qwen3DFlash2.compute_candidates ->
LogitsProcessor.get_top_k_tokens -> _topk -> _flashinfer_topk -- and that call exists in
both v0.28.0 and v0.29.0.

The consequence is a boot failure, not a slowdown. flashinfer 0.6.18's JIT emits
--compress-mode=size, which nvcc older than 13.0 rejects; 0.6.16.post3's does not emit it,
which is why the same code is harmless on the 0.28 line. No flashinfer-cubin release has
ever carried top-k (checked 0.6.13 and 0.6.18: zero topk artefacts in a 6.3 GB, 85,496-file
package), so the JIT is unavoidable for this op and a matching cubin does not rescue it.
vLLM's own wheel pins flashinfer-python==0.6.18 in Requires-Dist on 0.29.0, so pinning back
to 0.6.16.post3 fights the wheel. SPEC=dflash2 is the only line that reaches the call, which
is why SPEC=off and mtp boot on the same box (syv-ai/qwen38-27b-rtx3090#106).

The default is unchanged: the knob is bool = True, and =0 is the explicit opt-out, so this
only affects a run that already asked FlashInfer not to be used for sampling.

Measured on an RTX 3090, 0.29 image, cold FlashInfer cache, with a stub nvcc that always
exits 1 with "nvcc fatal : Unknown option '--compress-mode=size'". Only the switch differs:

  VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=1  ->  flashinfer.top_k,  _topk FAILED (JIT build)
  VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0  ->  None (torch.topk), _topk SUCCEEDED

Env knobs this patch reads go through vllm.envs: VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER (registered
upstream; this patch registers nothing new).

